From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:11:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/32] style(deacon): use the if-form for the FROZEN dedupe
 guard (gcp-llja)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Self-review touch-up. Step 3b's dedupe guard was written as
`[ -f "$MARK" ] && continue`, while the STALE escalation directly above it —
the block this one is modelled on — uses `if [ -f "$MARK" ]; then ... fi`.
These blocks are prose the deacon copies and runs, so the two guards reading
differently invites the reader to wonder whether the difference is meaningful.
It is not; match the neighbour.
---
 gastown/formulas/mol-deacon-patrol.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gastown/formulas/mol-deacon-patrol.toml b/gastown/formulas/mol-deacon-patrol.toml
index 297e9b2..baaed4b 100644
--- a/gastown/formulas/mol-deacon-patrol.toml
+++ b/gastown/formulas/mol-deacon-patrol.toml
@@ -576,7 +576,7 @@ cycle commits a bead per cycle), and dedupe so it is said once per condition:
 printf '%s\\n' "$RESULT" | jq -r 'select(.verdict == "FROZEN") | [.scope, .detail] | @tsv' |
 while IFS=$'\\t' read -r SCOPE DETAIL; do
     MARK="$GC_CITY/.gc/runtime/dolt-push-frozen-$SCOPE"
-    [ -f "$MARK" ] && continue
+    if [ -f "$MARK" ]; then continue; fi
     mkdir -p "$(dirname "$MARK")"
     gc session nudge mayor/ "Dolt push-state watermark frozen on $SCOPE (pushes ARE landing; bd is recording success as failure). Raise dolt.auto-push-timeout in $SCOPE's .beads/config.yaml — until then auto-push outage detection is blind on that store. $DETAIL"
     date -u +"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" >"$MARK"
-- 
